# Paths that DO NOT trigger CI / CD when they're the only thing changed
# in a PR or push. Lives at the repo root by convention (mirrors
# .gitignore / .dockerignore). Used by .github/actions/detect-code-changes/
# — both .github/workflows/ci.yml and .github/workflows/cd.yml read it.
#
# Despite the name, syntax is NOT gitignore — it's egrep (POSIX extended
# regex), one pattern per line, matched against the full path from the
# repo root. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored. Kept
# as regex because the workflow's bash already supports it with no deps.
#
# Add a pattern here when you want changes to those paths to skip the
# unit-tests + e2e + deploy + canary pipeline (they'll still record a
# green check so branch protection is satisfied).
#
# Be CONSERVATIVE — anything that affects runtime behavior must NOT be
# in this list:
#   slack-manifests/*.json — scope changes affect the running bot
#   .github/workflows/*.yml — workflow changes need verification
#   package.json / bun.lock — dep changes
#   Dockerfile / entrypoint.sh — image changes
# Those will still fall through to the full pipeline by virtue of NOT
# matching anything here.

# Markdown anywhere (CLAUDE.md, SPEC.md, README.md, SETUP.md, skill
# SKILL.md files, doc additions in any subdir).
\.md$

# Top-level non-code files.
^LICENSE$
^\.gitignore$
^\.env\.example$

# Operator-only box-provisioning script; never runs in the prod image.
^install\.sh$

# Operator-only host watchdog (deployed by install.sh); not in the prod image.
^scripts/canary-monitor\.sh$

# Host-served web content (status page under ~/apps/, served by Caddy); never
# in the prod bot image, so changes here skip e2e+deploy+canary.
^apps/

# Operator-only per-agent web app server: the systemd --user unit installed by
# install.sh and the Python server it runs. Host-local only, never in the prod
# bot image.
^systemd/
^webserver/
